#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:6
msgid "Unpin trait"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:8
msgid ""
"`Unpin` type allows types to move freely, even when they're wrapped by a "
"`Pin`"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:9
msgid "Most types implement `Unpin`, because it is an \"`auto trait`\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:10
msgid "`auto trait` behavior can be changed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:11
msgid "`!Unpin` types must never move"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:12
msgid ""
"Types containing a `PhantomPinned` field do not implement `Unpin` by default"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:16
msgid ""
"Explain that when a trait implements `Unpin`, the pinning behavior of "
"`Pin<Ptr>` does not get invoked. The value is free to move."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:19
msgid ""
"Explain that almost all types implement `Unpin`; automatically implemented "
"by the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:22
msgid ""
"Types implementing `Unpin` are saying: 'I promise I have no self-references, "
"so moving me is always safe.'"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:25
msgid "Ask: What types might be `!Unpin`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:27
msgid "Compiler-generated futures"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:28
msgid "Types containing a `PhantomPinned` field"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:29
msgid "Some types wrapping C++ objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md:31
msgid "`!Unpin` types cannot be moved once pinned"
msgstr ""
